# SLA-Aware Multi-Metric Autoscaling for Cloud-Native Applications

An SLA-aware Kubernetes autoscaling framework that combines **KEDA**, **Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)**, **Prometheus**, **Grafana**, and **AWS Serverless Services** to improve application reliability and maintain Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance under dynamic workloads.

This project was developed as part of the **MSc in Cloud Computing** at the **National College of Ireland (NCI)**.

---

## Project Overview

Traditional Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) primarily relies on CPU utilization, which is often insufficient for handling real-world workload variations. Applications may experience increased latency, request failures, or reduced responsiveness even when CPU usage remains low.

This project introduces an **SLA-aware multi-metric autoscaling framework** that makes scaling decisions using multiple Service Level Indicators (SLIs), improving responsiveness, resource utilization, and overall application availability.

Additionally, a **serverless fallback mechanism** ensures that incoming requests are not lost when Kubernetes services become unavailable or exceed SLA thresholds.

---

## Features

- Multi-Metric Autoscaling using KEDA
- Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)
- Amazon EKS Deployment
- FastAPI SLA Gateway
- FarmEase Cloud-Native Application
- Prometheus Metrics Collection
- Grafana Monitoring Dashboard
- Serverless Fallback using Amazon SQS and AWS Lambda
- Jenkins CI/CD Pipeline
- Docker Containerization
- Load Testing using K6
- Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR)

---

# System Architecture

```
                    Users
                      │
                      ▼
          AWS Network Load Balancer
                      │
                      ▼
             FastAPI SLA Gateway
                      │
        ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
        │                           │
        ▼                           ▼
   FarmEase Application      Serverless Fallback
    (Amazon EKS)              Amazon SQS Queue
        │                           │
        ▼                           ▼
   Kubernetes Pods            AWS Lambda Function
        │
        ▼
  KEDA + Horizontal Pod Autoscaler
        │
        ▼
 Prometheus Metrics Collection
        │
        ▼
     Grafana Dashboard
```

